## How the repositories connect — files created at each step

The application repository contains your code and tests. The three platform
repositories store enrollment requests, provisioning logic, and approved
Bitrise workflows.

**Gold-bordered boxes identify repositories. Blue boxes identify files or
file groups.**

| Step | File or output | Location | Responsible owner |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Application source, native projects, and dependency lockfiles | Application repository | Approved starter or application team. |
| 2 | `campfile.yml` | Application repository root | Developer, using the confirmed CAMP schema. |
| 3 | Tests and required test scripts | Application repository | Developer, using the existing test framework. |
| 4 | Approved workflow definitions and catalog metadata | `mobile-platform-configuration-bitrise-template` | Platform Engineering maintains these; developers select an approved template/version. |
| 5 | `Config/Teams/<team>/Bitrise/Apps/<app>.yaml` | `mobile-platform-configuration` | Developer creates the secret-free enrollment request. |
| 6 | Validation results and creation preview | Vela PR run | Platform automation produces these run outputs. |
| 7 | Bitrise application, repository connection, workflows, access, and protected bindings | External platform configuration | The approved provisioning engine applies the request after protected promotion. |
| 8 | Application binaries, matching test packages, and reports | Build outputs | The selected Bitrise workflows and repository commands. |
| 9 | Device-test results, security assessment, and delivery evidence | Approved service and build results | Configured integrations produce evidence for the exact candidate. |

