### What developers create

Prepare the application files, tests, `campfile.yml`, and enrollment request.
Use the approved schema and template version. The team directory must match
`team`, and the request filename must match `app_name`.

Platform Engineering maintains the provisioning engine and workflow catalog.
Protected credentials are supplied through approved bindings, not committed
inside the enrollment YAML.

### What happens after enrollment

The approved request provisions the Bitrise application once and attaches its
selected workflow configuration. Later application changes use the existing
enrollment and configured build triggers.

The selected template defines actual step order, concurrency, signing,
and destination behavior. QA/UAT route names do not automatically mean
public store delivery.

This flow does not establish that enrollment creates `bitrise.yml` inside
the application repository. Confirm any generated-file behavior with the
approved engine contract.
